Package: sparky-stereo-phone-camera
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, python3, droidcam, v4l2loopback-dkms, v4l2loopback-utils, adb, scrcpy, pkexec
Suggests: kdeconnect
Description: a phone as the computer's camera: DroidCam or scrcpy
 Sets up a virtual camera named "Phone camera" and starts either DroidCam's client (the DroidCam app on the phone, by Wi-Fi
 or USB) or scrcpy's camera mode (USB debugging, no app on the phone). The phone's camera is then a camera of the session:
 PipeWire lists it and System Settings, Camera shows it like any camera.
 .
 When something is missing (no phone found, the virtual camera module not built for the running kernel, Secure Boot refusing
 the module, USB debugging not allowed on the phone) the command says what and what to do, in the person's language.
 .
 KDE Connect is not needed: if it is installed it may find the phone, the stream never depends on it.
